2. Codex app-server protocol contract

   services/codex_runtime/codex_runtime/contract/*.json are JSON Schema files produced by
   `codex app-server generate-json-schema` from a pinned build of the Codex CLI
   (https://github.com/openai/codex). They derive from that project's protocol definitions,
   which are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
   (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). They are kept in this repository to pin the
   interface the code is written against. To regenerate them, run
   `python -m codex_runtime.generate_contract` from services/codex_runtime.

3. noVNC (downloaded, not included)

   infra/novnc/fetch_novnc.py downloads the release pinned in versions.lock.toml, and checks its
   SHA-256, while the stream gateway image is built. noVNC (https://github.com/novnc/noVNC) is
   licensed mainly under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, with some files under other licenses;
   see its repository.

4. Chrome for Testing (downloaded, not included)

   infra/browser/fetch_chrome.py downloads the pinned build for the browser capsule image. It is
